<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad Falihi Kaimuddin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1960</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad Falihi Kaimuddin was the last sultan of Buton, an island sultanate off south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, reigning from 1937 until his death in 1960. Buton had kept internal autonomy under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> rule since its alliance with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> in 1613. After his death no successor was installed, and the sultanate's lands became regencies of Southeast Sulawesi.</p></div>
